request.description:
Everything the contest's participants did, merged in time order: `query`, `answer`, `sign_in`, `sign_out`, `sign_in_failed`, `disqualified`, `started`, `finished`, `page_left`, `paste`, `ip_changed`, `parallel_session`, `tab_created`, `tab_renamed`, `tab_deleted`. Items come oldest first on every page.

- no cursor: the newest page;
- `after=<cursor>`: what came after it — the live screen polls with the page's `newest`; the newest 2 seconds are held back until the next poll, so an item written late with an earlier time is not skipped;
- `before=<cursor>`: what came before it — scroll back with the page's `oldest`.

`more` says there is more in the direction read. `kinds` (comma-separated), `participant` (a registration of this contest), `from` and `until` (RFC 3339, `[from, until)`), `limit` (at most 200). A cursor names a time between 2000 and 2200. Sign-ins count from the registration to an hour past the participant's finish or the contest's end.

Responses: 200 · 400 `monitor_invalid_cursor` / `monitor_invalid_filter` · 404 `monitor_participant_not_found` (another contest's registration, or none) · 401 · 403 · 429 `monitor_too_often`
